    {
      "id": "b41d7e25-6c3a-4f98-a0e1-5d2c7b9f0010",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -500,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 440,
        "height": 880,
        "content": "## Track new job openings at target companies in Google Sheets\n\n**Who it's for:** recruiters, sales teams selling to hiring companies, job seekers and market researchers who follow a list of companies and want every new opening the day it is posted.\n\n### How it works\n1. Every morning, **ATS Career Site Jobs** (tidytools/ats-career-site-jobs on Apify) reads the job boards of your companies: Greenhouse, Lever, Ashby, Workable, Workday, SmartRecruiters, Recruitee, Personio and more. A company website such as `stripe.com` is enough; the board is found for you.\n2. `onlyNewJobs` remembers every job per monitor name, so only openings that were not there yesterday come back.\n3. Each new job becomes one row in Google Sheets: company, title, location, department, remote, salary (when listed), posted date and link.\n\n### Setup\n1. Add your Apify credential (API key or OAuth) to the Apify node.\n2. In **Companies to track**, list the companies, optional title keywords and a monitor name.\n3. Choose your spreadsheet and sheet in **Append new jobs to Google Sheets**.\n\nThe first run returns all current jobs (they become the baseline). After that, only new ones.\n\n### Cost\n$1 per 1,000 jobs returned (Apify pay-per-event, Sept 2026). Unchanged, filtered-out and closed jobs are free. The Apify node has a $1 cost cap.\n\nUses the verified Apify community node (`@apify/n8n-nodes-apify`)."
      }
    },
